body:
You have a `prebuild:ssr` step that is running `ngcc`. This is trying to process every format of every entry-point of every package in `node_modules`. In particular it is trying to process the UMD format of `@ngneat/transloco`.

When ngcc is asked to process a UMD format it has to check every exported function in the file to see if it a `ModuleWithProviders` function. In this case this package exports the `flatten()` function, which is simply a wrapper for the default export of the `flat` library:

```ts
    function flatten(obj) {
        return flat(obj, { safe: true });
    }
```

Normally when ngcc comes across an external import like this it only needs to look at the typings file for the import and doesn't actually flow into the source code. But in this case `flat` does not have any typings, so we end up traversing into the source of the `flat` library. As far as ngcc is concerned it thinks that the source files from `flat` it is processing are part of the same entry-point as `@ngneat/transloco` and so it assumes (incorrectly that the file is UMD format). In this case `flat` is actually in CommonJS format, which doesn't have the correct shape for UMD - and so we come to the error.
